#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:16
msgid "Arduino Program Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:18
msgid "Let's take a look at the new sketch file. Although it has a few lines of code itself, it is actually an \"empty\" sketch. Uploading this sketch to the development board will cause nothing to happen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:33
msgid "If we remove ``setup()`` and ``loop()`` and make the sketch a real ``blank`` file, you will find that it does not pass the verification. They are the equivalent of the human skeleton, and they are indispensable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:36
msgid "During sketching, ``setup()`` is run first, and the code inside it (inside ``{}``) is run after the board is powered up or reset and only once. ``loop()`` is used to write the main feature, and the code inside it will run in a loop after ``setup()`` is executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:39
msgid "To better understand setup() and loop(), let's use four sketches. Their purpose is to make the on-board LED of the Arduino blink. Please run each experiment in turn and record their specific effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:41
msgid "Sketch 1: Make the on-board LED blink continuously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:59
msgid "Sketch 2: Make the on-board LED blink only once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:77
msgid "Sketch 3: Make the on-board LED blink slowly once and then blink quickly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:99
msgid "Sketch 4: Report an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:118
msgid "With the help of these sketches, we can summarize several features of ``setup-loop``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:120
msgid "``loop()`` will be run repeatedly after the board is powered up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:121
msgid "``setup()`` will run only once after the board is powered up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:122
msgid "After the board is powered up, ``setup()`` will run first, followed by ``loop()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:123
msgid "The code needs to be written within the ``{}`` scope of ``setup()`` or ``loop()``, out of the framework will be an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/05_basic_code_struct.rst:126
msgid "Statements such as ``digitalWrite(13,HIGH)`` are used to control the on-board LED, and we will talk about their usage in detail in later chapters."
msgstr ""
